<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Zagreb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a> is the oldest and largest university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. It traces its origins to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> academy founded in 1669 and was opened as a modern university in 1874, with faculties of law, theology and philosophy, with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-juraj-strossmayer">Josip Juraj Strossmayer</a>. It has been a centre of Croatian scholarship and national life ever since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-zagreb.jpg" alt="University of Zagreb" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sveučilište u Zagrebu · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UniZg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
